Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||10-24-2000||01:50 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.ls1.com/images/fe03s.jpg"> <P>I saw this on <A HREF="http://www.ls1.com" TARGET=_blank>www.ls1.com</A>  and wondered exactly what purpose it serves, and if something like it would be of use to a Fiero?<P> <A HREF="http://www.ls1.com/link_exhaust.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ls1.com/link_exhaust.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||sdm1964||10-24-2000||07:21 AM||||It is a cross over pipe. It is used to equal out the pressure on dual exaust. Helps remove exaust and give you a few more HP. Would not help us since we do not have true duel exaust||||reg||7
Z||000002||1FST2M6||10-24-2000||09:03 AM||||Lingenfelter, SLP (FireHawk, SS camaro) and MTI and a host of others that make cars fast have done LOST of research and if you notice they ALL run larger single exhaust. humm.. wonder why...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  the X or H pipe does what sdm said but even with true dual exhaust you'll be fighting yourself for torque... just like the headers i had, some times there is a pipe thats to big... just wish a muffler manufacrure would make an non cross flow muffler for our cars. (or Camaro etc..)  <P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||ThatRickGuy||10-24-2000||10:07 AM||||The reason why factory cars run larger single is purly emission based. 2 smaller exhaust pipes will flow much better, the x-pipe is the best design. The only problem with the dual exhaust style is getting enough heat to get the cats to work. To get a dual exhaust car to pass emmissions is hard as heck (at least if you're trying on a newer car), that's why you get residency in a county that doesn't have inspections, drop the cat and just run your pipes how you like  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I know my exhaust replacement will be cat-less, if not for the extra hp, then just because it's cheaper! ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||10-24-2000||12:11 PM||||I have seen that in the LS1 Vette forum. At least for the C5 Vette the main purpose is just sound. The stock C5 exaust sound is not mean enough. Do that mod (on both sides) and at WOT it sounds like a V8 should. Out of WOT it is not anoying. Its cheaper (+/- $60) than changing to a Brola or Corsa system ($800-$1K).||||reg||1
